{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix implemented and pushed for review: Gerrit change 1363 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1363), commit 5a4758cdf4. Change: keyword-only quiet=False on resolve_ticket_id (src/rebar/_ids.py) gating the three stderr ambiguity diagnostics; _referencing_commit_exists passes quiet=True for its history-scan candidates only. RED->GREEN evidence: new tests/unit/test_transition_close.py failed pre-fix (2 failed: ambiguity noise on stderr in both the found and not-found directions), passes post-fix (3 passed); mutation check (reverting quiet=True) returns the tests to RED. Gate decisions unchanged both directions: scan returns True for the full-ID trailer, False for an unreferenced id, identical pre/post fix. Explicit ambiguous-prefix resolution (no quiet) still prints its diagnostic (AC3). Targeted suites green (85 passed: close-gate subtree/heldout, completion gate, verify-commit-ticket, path-injection guards); make lint + make typecheck clean. Sibling sweep: verify_commit.py:106, descendants.py:83, bugfix_size_gate.py:159, artifact_emit.py:134 all resolve refs the user/author directly supplied (single commit or CLI arg), not a history-wide scan -- no siblings; parity holds because CLI/MCP/library closes all route through the same transition_close core."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785858650278922001,"uuid":"5a71ac86-439d-419b-9ab8-a979609acd03"}